{
    "post_id": 67795,
    "title": "קמע למכשירים שבורים | Amulet bowl formula for exorcising broken or malfunctioning electrical appliances",
    "author": "Isaac Gantwerk Mayer",
    "coauthors": [
        {
            "name": "Isaac Gantwerk Mayer",
            "bio": "From a family of musicians, Isaac Gantwerk Mayer believes that creative art is one of the most powerful ways to get in touch with the divine. He composes music and poetry in Hebrew and English. (He also <a href=\"/index.php?user_ID=342\">translates</a> and <a href=\"/index.php?user_ID=820\">transcribes</a> Hebrew and Aramaic texts, adding <em>niqqud</em> and <em>t'amim</em> as needed.) Isaac runs a Jewish music transcription service, which will transcribe and set any Jewish music in any language, recorded or written. Contact his service on <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/pg/isaacgmayerjewishtranscription/\">Facebook</a> or via <a href=\"https://igmjewishcreativeworks.com/contact\">his music blog</a>.",
            "website": "https://igmjewishcreativeworks.com",
            "avatar": "https://opensiddur.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/isaac-gantwerk-mayer-2021-e1674561264977-96x96.jpg",
            "profile_link": "https://opensiddur.org/profile/isaac-gantwerk-mayer"
        }
    ],
    "date": "2026-06-18",
    "last_updated": "2026-07-29",
    "excerpt": "A friend of mine moving into a new apartment complained that his washing machine was infested by demons. So I made this amulet in the style of the Babylonian magic bowl corpus (specifically, mostly based on the form of JBA 26 (MS 1928/43)) to help him. Then I was asked to upload my amulet text here so I generalized it a bit, vocalized it, and added gender instructions. For maximum efficacy, the text should be written in a spiral pattern in the concave side of an unglazed ceramic bowl and buried face-down at the threshold of your apartment. That being said, my friend just printed the included image out, and the technician managed to find the problem pretty quickly.\r\n",
    "content": "<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">\nA friend of mine moving into a new apartment complained that his washing machine was infested by demons. So I made this amulet in the style of the Babylonian magic bowl corpus (specifically, mostly based on the form of JBA 26 (MS 1928/43)) to help him. Then I was asked to upload my amulet text here so I generalized it a bit, vocalized it, and added gender instructions. For maximum efficacy, the text should be written in a spiral pattern in the concave side of an unglazed ceramic bowl and buried face-down at the threshold of your apartment. That being said, my friend just printed the included image out, and the technician managed to find the problem pretty quickly.</p>\n<p>Note: I’m using my original system for non-binary Aramaic declension.\n</p></div>\n<hr />\n<table style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" class=\"draggable toggleable-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th id=\"x\" style=\"text-align: right;\">Source (Jewish Babylonian Aramaic)</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Source (English)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"tmr-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nאָסוּתָא מִן־שְׁמַיָּא<br />\nלְבֵיתֵיהּ / לְבֵיתַהּ / לְבֵיתוֹהוֹי\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nHealing from heaven<br />\nto the home,\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"tmr-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n&nbsp;<br />\nאִתְּתֵיהּ / אִתְּתַהּ / אִתְּתוֹהוֹי <span class=\"instruction\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nאִינְשֵׁיהּ / אִינְשַׁהּ / אִינְשׁוֹהוֹי <span class=\"instruction\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nזוּגֵיהּ / זוּגַהּ / זוּגוֹהוֹי <span class=\"instruction\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<span class=\"instruction\">Married:</span><br />\n<span class=\"instruction\">to a man:</span> wife,<br />\n<span class=\"instruction\">to a woman:</span> husband,<br />\n<span class=\"instruction\">to non-binary:</span> partner,\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"tmr-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n&nbsp;<br />\nבְּרַתֵּיה / בְּרַתַּהּ / בְּרַתּוֹהוֹי <span class=\"instruction\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nבְּנָתֵיהּ / בְּנָתָהָא / בְּנָתוֹהוֹי <span class=\"instruction\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nבְּרֵיהּ / בְּרַהּ / בְּרוֹהוֹי <span class=\"instruction\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nבְּנוֹהִי / בְּנָהָא / בְּנוֹהוֹי <span class=\"instruction\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<span class=\"instruction\">with kids:</span><br />\n<span class=\"instruction\">one girl:</span> daughter,<br />\n<span class=\"instruction\">multiple girls:</span> daughters,<br />\n<span class=\"instruction\">one boy:</span> son,<br />\n<span class=\"instruction\">multiple, not all girls:</span> children,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_1');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_1');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[1]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_1\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Literally: sons, but in the plural used to refer to all children&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_1', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"tmr-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nקִנְיָנֵיהּ / קִנְיָנַהּ / קִנְיָנוֹהוֹי\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\npossessions,\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"tmr-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n&nbsp;<br />\nוּמַכְבְּסֵיהּ / וּמַכְבְּסַהּ / וּמַכְבְּסוֹהוֹי <span class=\"instruction\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nוּמַחְשְׁבֵיהּ / וּמַחְשְׁבַהּ / וּמַחְשְׁבוֹהוֹי <span class=\"instruction\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nוּמַזְגְּנֵיהּ / וּמַזְגְּנַהּ / וּמַזְגְּנוֹהוֹי <span class=\"instruction\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nוּרְחִיקָּלֵיהּ / וּרְחִיקָּלַהּ / וּרְחִיקָּלוֹהוֹי <span class=\"instruction\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nוְתַנּוּרֵיהּ / וְתַנּוּרַהּ / וְתַנּוּרוֹהוֹי <span class=\"instruction\">&nbsp;</span><br />\nוּמַדְּפְסֵיהּ / וּמַדְּפְסַהּ / וּמַדְּפְסוֹהוֹי <span class=\"instruction\">&nbsp;</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<span class=\"instruction\">broken or malfunctioning appliance:</span><br />\n<span class=\"instruction\">laundry unit:</span> and washer<br />\n<span class=\"instruction\">computer or wifi:</span> and computer<br />\n<span class=\"instruction\">air conditioner:</span> and AC<br />\n<span class=\"instruction\">phone:</span> and telephone<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_2');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_2');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[2]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_2\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> The word for “telephone” here, רְחִיקָּל, is an original coinage, combining רְחִיק far and קָל sound, as a calque of telephone (literally: far-sound). The words for washer, computer, and AC are adapted from modern Hebrew, since they are all in forms with Aramaic parallels. Ovens existed in ancient Babylon too so I just usted the same word for that one.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_2', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script><br />\n<span class=\"instruction\">oven, stove, microwave:</span> and oven<br />\n<span class=\"instruction\">printer, copier, scanner:</span> and printer\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"tmr-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nדְּפלוני בַּר־פלוני / בַּת־פלוני / בֵּי־פלוני\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nof [<span class=\"instruction\">name</span>] son / daughter / house of [<span class=\"instruction\">father’s name</span>]\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"tmr-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nחֲתִימָא וּמְחַתְּמָא בְּעִיזְקְתָא דְּיקוק צְבָאוֹת<br />\nרָזָא כִּיסִי הָדָא חַד רָזָא וְחַד גְּזָרָא<br />\nדְּגָזַר עֲלַיְכִי רִבִּי יְהוֹשֻׁעַ בֶּן־פְּרַחְיָא<br />\nקְבֵלַת שַׁמְתָּא דִּתְשַׁמְּתֵי<br />\nוּתְהוֹן בְּשַׁמְתָּא דְּרִבִּי יְהוֹשֻׁעַ בַּר־פְּרַחְיָא<br />\nוְתֶהֱוֵי בְּשַׁמְתָּא בִּשְׁמֵיהּ דְּאַשְׁמְדַי מַלְכָּא דְשֵׁדֵי<br />\nוְתֶהֱוֵי בְּשַׁמְתָּא בִּשְׁמֵיהּ דְּהוֹרְמִיז בַּר־לִילִּית<br />\nוְתֶהֱוֵי בְּשַׁמְתָּא בִּשְׁמֵיהּ דְּרַב יוֹסֵף שֵׁדָא<br />\nוְתֶהֱוֵי בְּשַׁמְתָּא בִּשְׁמֵיהּ דְּשִׁיבְתָּא<br />\nוְתֶהֱוֵי בְּשַׁמְתָּא בִּשְׁמֵיהּ דְּמִשַּׁבְרִירֵי שַׁבְרִירֵי בְּרִירֵי רִירֵי יְרֵי רֵי<br />\nוְתֶהֱוֵי בְּשַׁמְתָּא דְּכָל שֵׁדֵי וְחִישִּׁיכֵי לִילִין וְלֵילְיָתָא<br />\nדּאִית בְּאַרְעָא דְּיִשְׂרָאֵל וּדְאִית בְּבָבֶל\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nSealed and signed with the signet of <span class=\"divine-referent\">YQWQ of Hosts</span>,<br />\nthis hidden secret is one secret and one decree<br />\nthat Rabbi Yehoshua ben Peraḥya decreed against you.<br />\nYou have received the ban that you will be banned,<br />\nand ye will be in the ban of Rabbi Yehoshua bar Peraḥya,<br />\nand you will be in the ban in the name of Asmodeus king of demons,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_3');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_3');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[3]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_3\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Referred to as such in Pesachim 110a and Gittin 68a, this demon is first mentioned in the book of Tobit, and probably derives from the Avestan phrase aēšma-daēva = wrath-demon.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_3', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script><br />\nand you will be in the ban in the name of Hormiz son of Lilith,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_4');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_4');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[4]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_4\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> See Bava Batra 73a:11. The name “Hormiz” probably derives from the Zoroastrian deity Ahura Mazda. This deity is, in Zoroastrian contet, seen as a good deity. Some texts of the Gemara read “Hormin,” which may derive from the Zoroastrian evil deity Ahriman. Lilith is in this context simply the primordial mother-demon.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_4', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script><br />\nand you will be in the ban in the name of Rav Yosef the Demon,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_5');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_5');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_5\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[5]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_5\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> See Pesachim 110a and Eruvin 43a. Yosef the Demon, who used his mystical powers to go from study hall to study hall, is not referred to as a rabbi in the Gemara but is so in the magic bowl literature, perhaps on account of being mixed up with the human Rav Yosef.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_5').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_5', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script><br />\nand you will be in the ban in the name of Shivta,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_6');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_6');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_6\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[6]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_6\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> See Taanit 20b, Yoma 77b, and Chullin 107b. Shivta is the demon that infests unwashed hands.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_6').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_6', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script><br />\nand you will be in the ban in the name of Mishavriri Shavriri Briri Riri Iri Ri,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_7');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_7');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_7\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[7]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_7\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> See Pesachim 112a and Avodah Zarah 12b. Mishavriri Shavriri Briri Riri Iri Ri, also known as Shavriri for short, is the demon of blindness. This is the source of the video game Elden Ring’s “Shabriri.”&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_7').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_7', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script><br />\nand you will be in the ban of all demons and darknesses, lilin and liliths,<br />\nthat are in the land of Israel and that are in Babylonia.<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_8');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_8');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_8\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[8]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_8\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Here a synecdoche for the diaspora as a whole.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_8').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_8', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"tmr-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nחֲתִימָא וּמְחַתְּמָא אַסְקוּפָתַי דִּילִי<br />\nפלוני בַּר־פלוני / פלונית בַּת־פלוני / פלונו בֵּי־פלוני<br />\nדַּד בְּשֵׁיר שֵׁירָא בְּזוֹם זִימְרָא<br />\nבְּעִיזְקְתָא דְּיׄוׄכׄבׄרׄ זׄיׄוׄאׄ מׄצׄפׄץׄ הׄשׄתׄפׄאׄ אׄכׄתׄרׄיׄאׄלׄ<br />\nמִן־שֵׁדִין וּמִן־דֵּוִין וּמִין־לִלִּין כּוּלְּהוֹן<br />\nמִן־שְׂעָרְהוֹן<br />\nפלוני בַּר־פלוני / פלונית בַּת־פלוני / פלונו בֵּי־פלוני<br />\nמִן־דְּמֵיהוֹן שַׁקְלִית לְחַתְּמְהוֹן<br />\nוּמִן־גְּלֵדְהוֹן שַׁקְלִית לְרַקְּעָה בְּהוֹן<br />\nשְׁבָע שְׁבָע נְקִיט צוּצִיתֵיהּ\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nSealed and signed, my threshold,<br />\n[<span class=\"instruction\">name</span>] son / daughter / house of [<span class=\"instruction\">father’s name</span>]<br />\npulled, bound with binding, chained with chain,<br />\nwith the signet of <span class=\"divine-referent\">YWKBR ZYWʾ</span><span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_9');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_9');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_9\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[9]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_9\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> A common divine name in the magic bowl literature.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_9').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_9', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"divine-referent\">MṢPṢ HŠTPʾ</span><span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_10');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_10');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_10\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[10]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_10\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> The divine name יהוה צבאות “The Cause of Hosts” in atbash cypher&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_10').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_10', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> <span class=\"divine-referent\">ʾKTRYʾL</span><span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_11');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_11');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_11\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[11]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_11\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> See Berakhot 7a&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_11').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_11', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script><br />\nfrom demons and daevas and lilin all.<br />\nFrom their hair —<br />\nfor [<span class=\"instruction\">name</span>] son / daughter / house of [<span class=\"instruction\">father’s name</span>] —<br />\nfrom their blood I take for sealing them,<br />\nand from their skin I take for patching them,<br />\nseven, seven, its tendril seized!\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h3>Source(s)</h3>\n<style>\n       .errordiv { padding:10px; margin:10px; border: 1px solid #555555;color: #000000;background-color: #f8f8f8; width:500px; }#advanced_iframe {visibility:visible;opacity:1;vertical-align:top;}.ai-info-bottom-iframe { position: fixed; z-index: 10000; bottom:0; left: 0; margin: 0px; text-align: center; width: 100%; background-color: #ff9999; padding-left: 5px;padding-bottom: 5px; border-top: 1px solid #aaa } a.ai-bold {font-weight: bold;}#ai-layer-div-advanced_iframe p {height:100%;margin:0;padding:0}#ai-div-container-advanced_iframe\n       {\n           position: relative;\n           width: 100%; max-width: 100%;}\n       #ai-div-loader-advanced_iframe\n       {\n          position: absolute;\n          z-index:1000;\n          margin-left:-33px;\n          left: 50%;   top: 150px;\n         }}\n       #ai-div-loader-advanced_iframe img\n       {\n          border: none;\n       }\n\t.ai-fullscreen {\n\t  position:fixed;\n\t  z-index:99999 !important;\n\t  top:0px !important;\n\t  left:0px !important;\n\t  margin:0px !important;\n\t  width:100% !important;\n\t  height:100% !important;\n\t}\n\t.ai-fullscreen-wrapper {\n\t  height: 100vh;\n\t}\n\t.ai-fullscreen-display-none {\n\t    display: none !important;\n\t}\n\t</style><script type=\"text/javascript\">var ai_iframe_width_advanced_iframe = 0;var ai_iframe_height_advanced_iframe = 0;function aiReceiveMessageadvanced_iframe(event) {if (event.origin !== 'https://archive.org') {return;}  aiProcessMessage(event,\"advanced_iframe\", \"true\",\"\",\"false\",\"false\");}if (window.addEventListener) {  window.addEventListener(\"message\", aiReceiveMessageadvanced_iframe);} else if (el.attachEvent)  {  el.attachEvent(\"message\", aiReceiveMessageadvanced_iframe);}var aiOnloadScrollTop=\"true\";var ai